    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d661">

                <pb facs="1189" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1065"/>

                <head>No. 657.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Fairchild.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-11-15"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 15,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 197.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 195, of the 2d
                    instant, relative to the charges on cargo required by the Spanish consul-general
                    at New York, I inclose a copy of a letter from Messrs. Nutter, Kimball &amp;
                    Co., of Portland, Me., in reference to like exactions by the consular officers
                    of His Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d661-a1.xml" xpointer="d661-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
